NAME
     stty - the terminal's settings

SYNOPSIS
     stty [-a] [SETTING...]
     reset
     clear

DESCRIPTION
     stty prints or changes the terminal line settings: echo, icanon,
     isig, the special characters (intr, erase, kill, eof), rows and
     columns, and the rest of termios. Called as reset it puts a
     confused terminal back the way it should be; called as clear it
     clears the screen.

OPTIONS
     -a   print everything, not only what differs from the usual

SEE ALSO
     tty(1), sh(1)
